  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1211 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nAs our next upper level system moves through the CWA, cloud\ncoverage is forecast to finally clear out leaving behind clear\nskies. No precipitation will be associated with this system on\nWednesday. Instead, strong southwesterly winds will continue \nacross area until the upper trough's departure. Warm air advection\nand clearing skies will allow temperatures to warm up into the \n60s for the rest of the workweek. Our next large scale trough on \nFriday looks to have a more limited source of moisture compared \nto previous model runs. As a result, PoPs have sharply decreased \nand precipitation looks less likely this week. By the weekend, a \ncold front looks to overtake the area and there's an increasing \nchances that temperatures could drop below freezing on Sunday \nmorning.\n\nRangel",
